Holy guacamole... my first hard challenge

You get two files
1) private.key
2) msg.enc

Through previous challenges, I knew that you'd have to run something to the msg.enc using the private key to decode the encryption.

Knowing this, I used Openssl's command:

openssl pkeyutl -decrypt -inkey private.key -in msg.enc -out decrypted_message.txt

However, it is not that simple... because I got this message:

Public Key operation error
803FB0F601000000:error:0180006C:bignum routines:BN_mod_inverse:no inverse:crypto/bn/bn_gcd.c:532:

SO, something is wrong. But what? Therefore, I run this command to check wtf is wrong with this key:

openssl rsa -in private.key -check -noout

It returns:

RSA key not ok
