I know. WTF is this? We're interested in the modulus actually. It's made up of two large prime numbers. Our "fix" is basically finding those two prime numbers.

I used this website to find the factors of the modulus (decimal)
https://factordb.com/

Oh yea, be sure to change the modulus key to decimal format becuase it's now in HEX.
OR you can run this command which returns the modulus (HEX).

openssl rsa -in private.key -modulus -noout

